[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3128042640","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108905#issuecomment-3128042640","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108905","id":3128042640,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc66ciSQ","user":{"login":"Squamto","id":25984337,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1OTg0MzM3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25984337?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Squamto","html_url":"https://github.com/Squamto","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Squamto/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Squamto/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Squamto/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Squamto/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Squamto/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Squamto/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Squamto/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Squamto/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Squamto/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-28T16:27:48Z","updated_at":"2025-07-28T16:27:48Z","body":"The issue is not the duplication, but the stencil mode itself. When setting the stencil mode to outline or x-ray it internally sets the render priority to 1 + the previous one and goes over the MAX.\nThis can be reproduced in the editor e.g. on a MeshInstance3D or via script.\n\nI am not sure, which material the code is targeting, because the render priority on the targeted Material stays the same.\nI think it is referring to an internal render_pass, but I am not sure.\n\n#109052 clamps the render priority, when modifying it whilst setting the stencil mode, but I am not sure, if that is the intended fix.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.githu